# Command dart

## What does this command do:

Dart programming language SDK CLI — run, compile, analyze, format, and manage Dart packages. Bundled inside the Flutter SDK; no separate install needed when Flutter is present.

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: Bundled with Flutter — install Flutter (see flutter cheat) and dart is available automatically.
```
ln -sfn ~/sdk/flutter/current/bin/dart ~/.local/bin/dart
```
For a standalone Dart SDK without Flutter:
```
mkdir -p ~/sdk/dart
curl -L -o ~/Downloads/dart-linux-<version>-release.tar.gz \
  https://storage.googleapis.com/dart-archive/channels/stable/release/<version>/sdk/dartsdk-linux-x64-release.zip
# Extract and symlink same as Flutter pattern
```

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/dart → ~/sdk/flutter/current/bin/dart

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://dart.dev/tools/dart-tool

## Command options

# Show version
dart --version

# --- Running ---

# Run a Dart script
dart run bin/main.dart

# Run with define constants
dart run --define=ENV=prod bin/main.dart

# Run a globally installed package tool
dart run build_runner build

# --- Compiling ---

# Compile to self-contained native executable
dart compile exe bin/main.dart -o dist/myapp

# Compile to JavaScript (for web, not Flutter web)
dart compile js bin/main.dart -o dist/main.js
dart compile js -O4 bin/main.dart -o dist/main.js     # max optimization

# Compile to WebAssembly
dart compile wasm bin/main.dart -o dist/main.wasm

# AOT snapshot (faster startup, needs Dart runtime)
dart compile aot-snapshot bin/main.dart

# JIT snapshot (development caching)
dart compile jit-snapshot bin/main.dart

# --- Code quality ---

# Analyze a directory (uses analysis_options.yaml if present)
dart analyze

# Analyze specific file
dart analyze lib/main.dart

# Format all Dart files in-place
dart format .

# Format and show diff without writing
dart format --output=none .

# Preview automated fixes (dry run)
dart fix --dry-run

# Apply automated fixes
dart fix --apply

# Fix specific diagnostic code only
dart fix --apply --code=prefer_final_locals

# --- Testing ---

# Run all tests
dart test

# Run specific test file
dart test test/my_test.dart

# Run tests matching a name pattern
dart test --name "login"

# Run with coverage (outputs to coverage/lcov.info)
dart test --coverage=coverage

# --- Packages (pub) ---

# Fetch dependencies
dart pub get

# Add a dependency
dart pub add http

# Add a dev dependency
dart pub add --dev lints

# Remove a dependency
dart pub remove http

# Upgrade all to latest compatible versions
dart pub upgrade

# Upgrade to breaking versions (rewrites pubspec.yaml bounds)
dart pub upgrade --major-versions

# Show outdated packages
dart pub outdated

# Show dependency tree
dart pub deps

# Publish package to pub.dev
dart pub publish

# Login to pub.dev
dart pub login

# --- Global packages ---

# Install a tool globally
dart pub global activate pana
dart pub global activate dart_style

# Run a globally installed tool
dart pub global run pana

# List globally installed packages
dart pub global list

# Deactivate (uninstall) a global package
dart pub global deactivate pana

# --- Project creation ---

# Create a new Dart console app
dart create myapp

# Create a package
dart create --template package mypackage

# Create a web app
dart create --template web-simple myweb

# List templates
dart create --list-templates

# --- Documentation ---

# Generate API docs (outputs to doc/api/)
dart doc

# --- DevTools ---

# Open Dart DevTools in browser
dart devtools

# --- Info ---

# Show diagnostics (SDK paths, env)
dart info
